<title>USA: Lockheed unit wins 5-year $41 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Lockheed unit wins 5-year $41 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>NASHUA, N.H. 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp's unit Sanders said Wednesday it won a five-year $41.4 million contract from Boeing Co to provide electronic countermeasures radio systems for the U.S. Air Force's upgrade program.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to start delivering the systems in March 1999.</p>
<p>A Sanders spokesman said the company is a subcontractor of Boeing's $216 million contract with the U.S. Air Force to upgrade defensive systems on the B-1B Lancer bomber.</p>
</text>
